The FDA or other regulatory agency’s policies may change, and additional government regulations may be enacted that could prevent, limit, or delay regulatory approval of our product candidates or require certain changes to the labeling or additional clinical work concerning the safety and efficacy of the product candidates. We cannot predict the likelihood, nature, or extent of government regulation that may arise from future legislation or administrative action in the US or abroad. If we are slow or unable to adapt to changes in existing requirements or the adoption of new requirements or policies, or if we are not able to maintain regulatory compliance, we may lose any marketing approval that we may have obtained, and we may not achieve or sustain profitability, which would harm our business. In addition, failure to comply with these regulatory requirements could result in significant penalties and delays.

